<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2701" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annŭus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		annus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That lasts a year or continues through a year</i>,
				<i>of a year's duration</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">penus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 2, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 6, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">provincia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 15, 14 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magistratus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 1, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Hann. 7, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imperium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					H. 3, 46 al.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spatium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 5, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cultura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 24, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annui victus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 46, 47, § 151</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That returns</i>, <i>recurs</i>, or
				<i>happens every year</i>, <i>yearly</i>, <i>annual.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: annuo in cursu, Att. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 20, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 618</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commutationes,</span>”
				<i>changes of the seasons</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labor (agricolarum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Verr. 2, 3, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plenitudo annuae messis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jer. 5, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deponit flavas annua terra comas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					2, 1, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annua magnae Sacra refer Cereri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 338</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annuos reditus non dabunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1</span></i>
			 Esdr. 4, 13: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annuā vice,</span>”
				<i>annually</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 8, 27, § 92</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annuis vicibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 20, 22, § 44 al.</span></i>
			—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annŭum</span></b> , i, and more freq. in
			the plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annŭa</span></b> , ōrum,
			n., <i>an annuity</i>, <i>annual stipend</i>, <i>pension</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">publici servi annua accipiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 10, 40</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Vesp. 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Tib. 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Gram. 3, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si cui annuum relictum fuerit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					33, 1, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">33, 1,
		10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
